@startuml
title NOTIFY — Real-Time Notification

skinparam dpi 300
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ArrowColor #64748B
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #CBD5E1
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam ActorBorderColor #3B82F6
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #94A3B8
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #F8FAFC

hide footbox
autonumber

actor "Authenticated User" as User
boundary "App Shell / WS Client" as UI
control "JwtChannelInterceptor" as Security
control "STOMP Broker" as Broker
control "NotificationService" as Service
control "NotificationRealtimePublisher" as Publisher

note over User, Security
  Preconditions: tenant ACTIVE; user already authenticated on REST;
  an inbox row has just been committed (dispatcher function).
  This function does not list, mark-read, or send SMTP.
end note

== Subscribe ==

User -> UI: Keep session open after login
activate UI
UI -> Security: CONNECT /ws (JWT)
activate Security

alt Missing or invalid JWT
  Security --> UI: Close connection
  deactivate Security
  UI --> User: Fall back to polling inbox later
else Authenticated
  Security -> Security: setCurrentTenant(tenant from token)
  Security -> Broker: Accept CONNECT
  activate Broker
  deactivate Security
  UI -> Broker: SUBSCRIBE /user/queue/notifications
  Broker --> UI: Subscribed

  == Push after inbox insert ==

  opt User session still subscribed
    Service -> Publisher: afterInboxInsert(notification)
    activate Service
    activate Publisher
    Publisher -> Broker: convertAndSendToUser(userId, payload)
    Broker -> UI: MESSAGE (id, type, title, deepLink)
    UI --> User: Toast / unread badge +1
    Publisher --> Service
    deactivate Publisher
    deactivate Service
  end

  == Client at-least-once ==

  opt Duplicate MESSAGE with same notification id
    UI -> UI: Ignore already rendered id
  end

  == Disconnect ==

  User -> UI: Leave workspace or token expires
  UI -> Broker: DISCONNECT
  Broker -> Broker: clear TenantContext
  deactivate Broker
  UI --> User: Realtime stopped
end

deactivate UI

note over Broker, Publisher
  At-least-once: broker may redeliver after reconnect.
  Client dedupes by notification id. Missed messages
  are recovered by GET /notifications, not by this channel.
end note

@enduml
